RF.put("questb:b44",{"8524":{"id":8524,"t":"The Alliance Needs Rainbow Fin Albacore!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 54.","obj":"Bring 20 Rainbow Fin Albacore to Slicky Gastronome at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Rainbow Fin Albacore","desc":"Hey there, friend! If I were to say to you, 'Don't you think that soldiers should have food to eat like anyone else?', you would of course reply, 'yes'. I agree with you 110%! I'm glad we're in accord. All I need for you to do is to head out there, fish up a whole bunch of raw rainbow fin albacore, and then cook it all up and bring it back to me right here. Mmm, mmm, I can taste it already.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"I'm willing to lay odds that you've returned with all of that rainbow fin albacore we were talking about before, right, ‹class›?","done":"Two for the Alliance, one for me, two for the Alliance, one for me. Hey there, fishmonger, excellent work. I can see that you're going to be a real credit to the club. Looks to me like we probably need more of that albacore though. Why don't you head on out and rustle up a mite more. I can hear my stomach rumbling already.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":32.3,"n":"Slicky Gastronome","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8604":{"id":8604,"t":"The Horde Needs Wool Bandages!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 55.","obj":"Bring 20 Wool Bandages to Healer Longrunner at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Wool Bandage","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. In preparation for the war at Ahn'Qiraj, I am here coordinating the Horde's efforts at gathering wool bandages. Unfortunately, out in the field, our soldiers cannot afford to rely upon the presence of a healer to keep them alive. Trust me, I know first hand. Thus, we're putting together all of these first aid kits for them.\nIf you have the time, I need many wool bandages. Return them to me here and I will see to it that you are properly rewarded.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"The dredge strikers are a serious threat and must be dealt with quickly!","done":"You have my sincere gratitude. Your efforts in helping Cenarion Hold have shown true courage.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.1,"y":74.2,"n":"Healer Longrunner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"7164":{"id":7164,"t":"Honored Amongst the Clan","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Frostwolf Insignia Rank 2","desc":"It is good to see you again, ‹class›. I had not expected you to return. Alas, you have proven yourself a brave and honorable soldier of the Frostwolf.\nYour time has come again, ‹name›. You have earned a new ranking and as such, a new insignia denoting this rise in stature.\nPresent your insignia.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostwolf Insignia Rank 3\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"It is good to see you again, ‹class›. I had not expected you to return. Alas, you have proven yourself a brave and honorable soldier of the Frostwolf.\nYour time has come again, ‹name›. You have earned a new ranking and as such, a new insignia denoting this rise in stature.\nPresent your insignia.","done":"<Warmaster Laggrond salutes.>\nGo, ‹name›! Continue your defense of the Frostwolf. This war must be won! For Drek'Thar! For the Warchief!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":62.3,"y":58.9,"n":"Warmaster Laggrond","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"684":{"id":684,"t":"Wanted!  Marez Cowl","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Wanted! Marez Cowl. New rewards: Wild Headdress, Stromgarde Bracers.","obj":"Bring Marez's head to Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe.\nMarez's Head Marez Cowl","desc":"A bounty has been placed on the head of Marez Cowl, a high-level advisor and operative of the Syndicate. She was last seen within the Syndicate controlled territory of Stromgarde.\nBounty may be collected from Captain Nials.\nBe warned: Marez is a skilled and cunning Warlock, known for her trafficking with demons. Extreme caution is advised when hunting her.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nArcane Runed Bracers Wild Headdress Stromgarde Bracers\nNew in Forever: Wild Headdress, Stromgarde Bracers.\nExperience: 3,750\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Greetings, ‹class›. You have a report to make?","done":"You took down Marez Cowl? Well done, ‹name›. Well done indeed!\nMarez menaced our Stromgarde defenders, and it is rumored she was an emissary between the Syndicate and some other, darker power. We are glad to see she'll longer ply her powers against us.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46,"y":47.8,"n":"Wanted Board","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":47.6,"n":"Captain Nials","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"3564":{"id":3564,"t":"Andron's Payment to Jediga","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Andron's Note to Jediga in Azshara.\nAndron's Note\nProvided: Andron's Note","desc":"Here... take... <hic> this to Jediga. Good luck to ya!","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,800","back":"Have you met with Andron yet? He rarely leaves Undercity, so I don't think it'd be too hard to find him.","done":"Perfect... wait a minute.\nHaha! What'd you tell him when you delivered the tablet, ‹name›? He overpaid us way too much! Not that I'm complaining. Did you tell him the deal changed? Or was he drunk again?\nDoesn't matter... here, take an extra share also.\nUndercity Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":54.8,"y":76.3,"n":"Andron Gant","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":22.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Jediga","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"4764":{"id":4764,"t":"Doomrigger's Clasp","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Doomrigger's Clasp to Mayara Brightwing in the Burning Steppes.\nDoomrigger's Clasp Doomrigger's Coffer","desc":"There is a chamber, high in Blackrock Spire, that was once called the Hall of Fortune. It was where the Dark Iron dwarves kept their relics, trophies and objects of art.\nThat was long ago. It is said the hall has collapsed and is now used for... less savory tasks. But I believe some old dwarven relics may still be found there.\nOne such relic is Doomrigger's clasp, with a surface so encrusted with rare gems that it was said to make weep any dwarf who gazes upon it.\nThat clasp, ‹name›, is your goal.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have the clasp, ‹name›? My patron will pay very handsomely for it.","done":"You found it! So the rumors were true!\nThank you, ‹name›. My patron, Count Remington Ridgewell, will be quite pleased to see this addition to this collection.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":84.8,"y":69.1,"n":"Mayara Brightwing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"2764":{"id":2764,"t":"Galvan's Finest Pupil","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Trenton Lighthammer in Gadgetzan.","desc":"If you are ready to conclude your training with Galvan, you should journey to Gadgetzan.\nThere, you will find my finest pupil: Trenton Lighthammer. He has much to teach you in the ways of ornate mithril. Otherwise, remain here and learn!\nOh, Gadgetzan is in Tanaris, of course!","rew":"Experience: 2,900","done":"Galvan the Ancient sent you??\n<Trenton bows.>\nIt is a great honor to meet another of the master's pupils!\nStranglethorn Vale Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":20.5,"n":"Galvan the Ancient","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.8,"n":"Trenton Lighthammer","e":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"2604":{"id":2604,"t":"Spiritual Domination","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring ten Vulture Gizzards and two Snickerfang Jowls to Bloodmage Lynnore.\n10 Vulture Gizzard Black Slayer 40 % , Spiteflayer 30 %\n2 Snickerfang Jowl Starving Snickerfang 40 % , Snickerfang Hyena 40 % , Ravage 30 %","desc":"I see that the inner fire has dwindled. Would you say the spiritual euphoria lasted an hour?\nIf it's more of the gizzard gum you desire, then more of the gizzards I require. Back to the wastelands, ‹name›. Do not return until you have recovered ten gizzards and two jowls.","rew":"You will receive:\nGizzard Gum","back":"Do not waste my time, ‹name›. We have nothing to discuss, unless you have recovered the items I have requested.","done":"Perhaps one day I shall be able to isolate the active enzymes of this assay and produce a much more efficient resultant. Unfortunately, you will have to settle for what I am currently able to produce. Return to me should you require more gizzard gum.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.3,"n":"Bloodmage Lynnore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"96044":{"id":96044,"t":"Camping 101 blacksmithing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Tognus Flintfire in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your blacksmithing skill to 20","desc":"So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Sharpening Wheel. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.2,"y":52,"n":"Tognus Flintfire","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"97964":{"id":97964,"t":"Camping 101 blacksmithing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Aedi Thriceforged in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your blacksmithing skill to 20","desc":"So, you've become a Blacksmith. That's a great choice if you want to make sure your blades never dull.\nI reckon I know someone that can help with that by teaching you how to craft a Sharpening Wheel. Bring one of these out at your camp and all the warriors and rogues in the area will be lining up to hone their weapons.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Sharpening Wheel. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.8,"y":44.4,"n":"Aedi Thriceforged","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"98284":{"id":98284,"t":"Camping 101 enchanting","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Nasalanna Windsinger in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your enchanting skill to 20","desc":"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.2,"y":43.2,"n":"Nasalanna Windsinger","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96604":{"id":96604,"t":"The great outdoors","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sit near Brakk's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.\nUse the /sit emote near the campfire\nGain the Boosted Rest buff","desc":"Greetings, ‹class›. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\nYou'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I'll walk you through it.","back":"Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.","done":"So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill from the trainers in the village nearby. They will also teach you how to create a camp fixture suitable to your new profession.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94284":{"id":94284,"t":"Craftsmans writ catseye ultra goggles","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Catseye Ultra Goggles\nCatseye Ultra Goggles","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Catseye Ultra Goggles, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Catseye Ultra Goggles Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94284","cats":["crafting"]},"7884":{"id":7884,"t":"Crocolisk Boy and the Bearded Murloc","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Turtle Scale Leggings","rew":"You will receive:\n12 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"Yebb is working on other attractions for his zoo, including wet, swampy abodes for a boy raised by crocolisks, and perhaps for a murloc. We will need nice, water-tight leggings so we won't get waterlogged during prop-ups and tear-downs. For that job, I think turtlescale leggings will do the trick.\n‹name›, can you make those leggings? If you do, then a fat stack of Darkmoon Faire tickets will be your reward...","done":"Great, you made them! These will do nicely... I just hope I won't be the one to clean the crocolisk cage when the time comes. Those beasts can be rather beastly, don't you think?\nHere are your tickets, ‹name›. Enjoy them, and enjoy your stay at the Darkmoon Faire!\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.6,"y":70.8,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.2,"y":42.5,"n":"Chronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"1484":{"id":1484,"t":"The Corrupter","lv":33,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 33 instead of 35.","obj":"Speak to Takata Steelblade in Desolace.","desc":"This creature is far more dangerous than I had anticipated. No doubt Takata questions my abilities to take on such a creature, and it would insult his honor if he were not informed about what just happened.\nSpeak to the swordsman, tell him you are willing to slay the demon if he would allow it, but do not press too hard. It is better if he thinks it his own idea.","rew":"Experience: 270","done":"I witnessed what just occurred with Maurin and the demon lord. That creature, even as an apparition, seems to have more power than my warlock companion. I wonder if he's up to the task of defeating the monster? It would serve the Warchief better if I go myself, but with my responsibilities here, I would disgrace my clan if I turned my back on my duties here to battle this evil for my own honor.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":52.2,"y":53.4,"n":"Maurin Bonesplitter","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":52.6,"y":54.4,"n":"Takata Steelblade","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7484":{"id":7484,"t":"Libram of Focus","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 54 instead of 58.","obj":"Bring a Libram of Focus, 1 Pristine Black Diamond, 4 Large Brilliant Shards, and 2 Skin of Shadow to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul to receive an Arcanum of Focus.\nLibram of Focus Prince Tortheldrin 2 % , Magister Kalendris 2 % , Illyanna Ravenoak 2 % , Tendris Warpwood 2 % and 4 more\nPristine Black Diamond Veteran Commando 2.3 % , Witherbark Speaker 1 % in Zul'Gurub , Winterax Axe Thrower 1 % , Lady Illucia Barov 1 % in Scholomance and 4 more\n4 Large Brilliant Shard\n2 Skin of Shadow Skin of Shadow , Lady Illucia Barov 19 % in Scholomance , Risen Bonewarder 17 % in Scholomance , Risen Construct 17 % in Scholomance and 3 more","desc":"This libram almost aroused interest in one of the younger Lorekeeper's familiars. Poor thing, it was only a few weeks old.\nThose among you who are more magically inclined might find this item interesting.\nThe Libram of Focus was lost in this wing. I can only assume one of the Highborne spirits holds it in their possession.\nBring the Libram along with some large brilliant shards, skin of shadow, and a pristine black diamond and I shall conjure the Arcanum.","rew":"You will receive:\nArcanum of Focus\nExperience: 1,650\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You again? What could you possibly want now?","done":"Don't hurt yourself when applying the enchantment, ‹race›.\nStart Lorekeeper Lydros End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7484","cats":["dire-maul"]},"6124":{"id":6124,"t":"Curing the Sick","lv":14,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Curative Animal Salve on 10 Sickly Deer that are located throughout Darkshore; doing so should cure them. Sickly Deer have been reported starting south of the Cliffspring River to the north of Auberdine and extending all the way into southern Darkshore where the edge of Ashenvale begins.\nSickly Deer cured : 0/ 10\nProvided: Curative Animal Salve","desc":"The amount of salve made out of the reagents you brought me is good enough for ten doses, ‹name›. While I work with the village to try and make some more salve, I'd like for you to help us get a head start. All around Darkshore are sickly deer; use the salve on them and cure their malaise.\nDendrite Starblaze in Moonglade will want to talk to you when you're done, I'm sure. Please extend Auberdine's thanks to the Cenarion Circle there... and let me say thanks to you directly for the help you've given!","rew":"You will receive:\nVeildust Medicine Bag\nExperience: 750\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Have you completed what was asked of you by Alanndarian Nightsong of Auberdine? Your work is not complete unless it is.","done":"You have done well in tending to the sickly deer of Darkshore; they are unwitting victims of a greater taint and corruption that is spreading all throughout the land. There are those in Darnassus who choose to recognize this threat... and there are those who ignore the growing signs. I hope you will not be one to put blinders on about what facts stare you in the face, ‹name›.\nRegardless, you've proven your worth as a friend of nature and the Circle - take this as a symbol of such.\nDarkshore Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.7,"y":40.7,"n":"Alanndarian Nightsong","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"924":{"id":924,"t":"The Demon Seed","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grab a Flawed Power Stone. Bring it to the Altar of Fire before the stone expires, then return to Ak'Zeloth.\nDestroy the Demon Seed","desc":"The Demon Seed is a powerful tool for the Burning Legion. It rests in a cave on Dreadmist Peak, above a demonic altar of fire.\nI have prepared power stones that when placed near the Seed will disrupt its connection to the Legion.\nTake a stone from the table and bring it to the altar of fire atop Dreadmist Peak. Travel west, then north when the road forks. The Peak will be to your left. The safest climb to the top is on its northern face.\nAnd hurry--the stone's power will consume itself in time.","rew":"You will receive:\nBanshee Armor\nExperience: 1,250\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"The Demon Seed still exists. I can sense its power...","done":"Your task is complete. You have destroyed the Demon Seed as Neeru bid. But this is not the end...\nThe destruction of the Demon Seed sent waves of power through the ether, waves of staggering force. I felt them, and I am sure other beings did as well. Others who will wonder why their toy was broken...\nBut regardless of future troubles, I have something for you. Neeru sent it as payment. And he bid me thank you.\nSo, thank you.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":20.1,"n":"Ak'Zeloth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"92124":{"id":92124,"t":"Book inventory","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Daniel, Brother Paxton's assistant in the library.","desc":"We need to take stock of how many books are missing!\nGo talk to my useless assistant, Daniel. He can do a quick inventory and let us know how serious the problem is.\nHe's obsessed with the various trade professions in Elwynn Forest. The boy keeps focusing on those instead of his important work helping me.\nDon't let him prattle on about tradeskills, and find out what's happened to my books!","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 0 silver, 3 copper Experience: 15\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Yah, I overheard. I warned Brother Paxton three times about the kobolds tunneling under the abbey.\nIt looks like the kobolds have taken a lot of books. There are whole bookshelves emptied out. You should probably see what Brother Paxton wants you to do about it.\nWhile you're here, can I talk to you about tradeskills? I'd be happy to answer any questions you have, or point you toward the local trainers.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.4,"y":40.4,"n":"Brother Paxton","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.4,"y":40.6,"n":"Daniel","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"91724":{"id":91724,"t":"Delicate instruments","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 6 Defias Rogue Wizards at Stone Cairn Lake, then return to Hamish Bergwort in the Tower of Azora.\nDefias Rogue Wizard slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Almost there, and... By the Nether! Something is still disrupting my instruments.\nThis is most frustrating, ‹name›. I have heard rumors that the local bandits have been practicing spells near Stone Cairn Lake. Maybe if you stop them, these disruptions will finally cease and I can get some work done?","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","done":"It seems like everything is working properly. Thank you, Chonk.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":65,"y":69.8,"n":"Hamish Bergwort","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3644":{"id":3644,"t":"Membership Card Renewal","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -2g instead of 0.","rew":"You will receive:\nGoblin Engineer Membership Card","back":"In order to renew your membership card, you will need to pay the renewal fee of two gold pieces.","done":"Since you're a practitioner of Goblin engineering and are in good standing, I am able to renew a lapsed membership card for the fee of two gold pieces. Once this fee is paid, you will be reissued a new membership card. This will allow access to Goblin engineering schemata from appropriate trainers.\nThis card will last for two weeks of activity, at the end of which your membership fees will become due again! If you want to access schemata, you'll need to bring your dues out of arrears.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.3,"n":"Nixx Sprocketspring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4444":{"id":4444,"t":"Corrupted Whipper Root","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a whipper root plant. The visible roots of the plant appear tough and leathery, and a slimy film hangs from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply 3 Cenarion Plant Salves to the Whipper Root. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":49.4,"y":12.2,"n":"Corrupted Whipper Root","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5884":{"id":5884,"t":"Salve via Gathering","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Fel Creep Sungrass 15 % , Mountain Silversage 15 % , Dreamfoil 15 % , Golden Sansam 15 % and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood's corruption. My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve.\nWhen you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.","done":"Excellent work ‹name› - every bit of this, once we purify it, will help us take back Felwood. Here, take some doses of Cenarion plant salve and head into the forest. The reclaiming of the land from the corruption waits for no ‹race›!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4124":{"id":4124,"t":"The Missing Courier","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold.","desc":"An associate of mine, Ginro Hearthkindle, is looking for assistance concerning the location of a courier and the parcels he was carrying. It has been a week or so since the courier went missing; our own searches have proved fruitless, and we're at an impasse. Unfortunately, I have had to declare the courier as missing in action.\nIf you have the time and resources to spare, please speak with Ginro. He should be here in the Stronghold - perhaps in his quarters.","rew":"Experience: 360","done":"Latro sent you to me, I presume. While I think it is a lost cause at this point, I'll take whatever assistance you can offer. I must admit... I'll be glad once I can put my mind to rest on this matter. Every day I set out into the wilds of Feralas looking for signs of Raschal, and every night I have come back with nothing to show for my work save gnoll teeth and disappointment.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.4,"y":46.2,"n":"Latronicus Moonspear","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":31.9,"y":45.1,"n":"Ginro Hearthkindle","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2844":{"id":2844,"t":"The Giant Guardian","lv":49,"min":44,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate the lost night elf girl.","desc":"I am no good, ‹name›. I was 'spose to be watchin' over my little friend, Shay, and somehow, she got away from me. I'm not all that sure what happened, really, but last time I saw her, we was walkin' through the ruins just north of here.\nEverythin' was goin' fine, but then I turned around, and... she was gone.\nNow I jus can't quite figure out what I should do here. Got any ideas, ‹name›? I'm awful worried.\nHey, how 'bout you go look fer Shay? Yer legs can travel much faster 'n mine.","rew":"Experience: 3,400","done":"Oh, I am so glad you found me! I must admit, I am a bit lost... But isn't this a beautiful place?","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":42.4,"y":22,"n":"Rockbiter","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":38.2,"y":10.3,"n":"Shay Leafrunner","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2924":{"id":2924,"t":"Essential Artificials","lv":30,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Essential Artificials to Klockmort Spannerspan in Ironforge.\n12 Essential Artificial Artificial Extrapolator","desc":"A nigh-universal mechanical component--the essential artificial--was of great use to the tinkers and smiths of Gnomeregan. But during the frantic exodus from our city, no one remembered to take any of these devices with them! And I need a large supply of them for work I will soon undertake.\nPlease, go into Gnomeregan and get me some essential artificials. You'll find them in the deeper areas of our city, held in containers called artificial extrapolators.\nThank you, ‹name›, and please hurry!","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Do you have the essential artificials?","done":"You got them! Now I can begin my new experiments!\nI can't thank you enough, ‹name›! Your bravery has advanced gnomish research by a leap and a bound!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62,"y":28.5,"n":"Klockmort Spannerspan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"4604":{"id":4604,"t":"More Sparklematic Action","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -1g -3s instead of 0.","obj":"Grime-Encrusted Object Holdout Technician 25 % , Holdout Medic 25 % , Holdout Warrior 25 % , Irradiated Pillager 25 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nSparklematic-Wrapped Box","back":"The Sparklematic 5200 is empty, awaiting a grime-encrusted object to clean and three silver coins to start!","done":"The Sparklematic 5200 comes to life, lurching to and fro. Inside, the helpless grime that has encrusted the object placed within it is being pulverized by the machine's gnomish cleaning agent.\nThe Sparklematic 5200 comes to a halt, heralded by a familiar \"ding!\" The item receptacle of the machine spirals open, revealing a neatly wrapped box.\nStart The Sparklematic 5200 End The Sparklematic 5200 Level 30 , requires level 25 Difficulty 25 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 4604\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 30, 2,450 XP in all.\n1 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nInsert a Grime-Encrusted Item into the Sparklematic 5200, and be sure to have three silver coins to start the machine.\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2 [ 30 ] The Sparklematic 5200!\nThe Sparklematic 5200\n2,450 XP\n3 [ 30 ] More Sparklematic Action this quest\nThe Sparklematic 5200","cats":["gnomeregan"]},"524":{"id":524,"t":"Elixir of Agony","lv":30,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,650 experience instead of 3,600, 1.01 times as much.","obj":"Place the Tainted Keg on the rug for the captured farmers.\nTainted Keg\nProvided: Tainted Keg","desc":"Next door the Deathguards are holding a few captured farmers hostage. High Executor Darthalia suspected one of the military strategists from Stormwind to be hiding out amongst them. Apparently the military chap was found dead in the Plaguelands last night. Darthalia, always looking out for me, decided the prisoners would be left to my disposal.\nI think it's time we threw those farmers a party. Sounds like a grand ol' time!\nPlace this tainted keg on the rug in their room. Plagued brew for all!","rew":"Experience: 3,650\n+200 reputation with Undercity","back":"A musty smell emanates from the rug.","done":"You rest the tainted deg on the dusty rug.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.8,"y":18.7,"n":"Dusty Rug","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"7804":{"id":7804,"t":"A Donation of Mageweave","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Mageweave Cloth Northshire Guard 54.5 % , Deep Dweller 48.4 % , Refuge Pointe Defender 40.7 % , Stonard Hunter 40.2 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Mageweave is running low, and we could use your help to replenish our stocks! By counting on the community as a whole, we would only need a donation of 60 pieces of mageweave cloth from you to enable us to reach our goal. Such generosity would not go unnoticed by Ironforge, I assure you!\nIf you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58,"y":26.2,"n":"Mistina Steelshield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"9004":{"id":9004,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Deliana your Shadowcraft Cap and Shadowcraft Tunic.\nShadowcraft Cap Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nShadowcraft Tunic General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"That's an amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved. Now maybe I'll be able to sleep at night with both eyes shut.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you'll really enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmantle Cap Darkmantle Tunic\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Shadowcraft pieces in exchange for your new Darkmantle Cap and Tunic?","done":"I'm going to miss you, ‹name›. I owe you such a debt of gratitude; I think I'll never be able to repay it.\nI hope that you enjoy your new head and chest armor, and that it protects you for a long time to come.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8684":{"id":8684,"t":"Dreamseer the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.6,"y":27,"n":"Elder Dreamseer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1884":{"id":1884,"t":"Ju-Ju Heaps","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy 4 Ju-Ju Heaps, then return to Un'thuwa in Sen'jin Village.\nJu-Ju Heaps Destroyed : 0/ 4","desc":"The warlock Zalazane of the Echo Isles has disrupted the normal flow of magic in Durotar. He does this through tainted fetishes, ju-ju heaps, which he has placed among his huts on the main Echo Isle.\nThese heaps corrupt our wildlife and give power to the warlocks and infernal creatures that lurk in the land's dark corners.\nYou must destroy the ju-ju heaps, ‹name›, before the flow of magic is forever altered.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLey Orb Ley Staff\nExperience: 850","back":"You must hurry, ‹name›. Destroy the ju-ju heaps!","done":"I sense that Zalazane's ju-ju heaps were destroyed, and with time, and luck, the flow of magic in Durotar will return to normal.\nA great deed you have done for your people, ‹name›. And you have shown your worth to us, the mages of the Horde.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":56.3,"y":75.1,"n":"Un'Thuwa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9324":{"id":9324,"t":"Stealing Orgrimmar's Flame","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 70s instead of 0. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 5,000, 0.99 times as much. No longer rewards Toasted Smorc, Midsummer Sausage, Fire-toasted Bun, Elderberry Pie.","obj":"Return the Flame of Orgrimmar to the Festival Loremaster.\nFlame of Orgrimmar\nProvided: Flame of Orgrimmar","desc":"This flame, stolen from the heart of Orgrimmar itself, floods you with warmth. This raw power is foreign to you, but the Loremaster might know more...","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Burning Blossom 10 Burning Blossom\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,950","back":"You're practically glowing, ‹race›. What do you have there?","done":"What's this? Unless I'm mistaken, this flame has been taken from the heart of Orgrimmar itself! The fierce hearts of the orcs and trolls are reflected in its searing heat. What a fine addition to our collection--how brave you are, stealing into the enemy's lair to retrieve the sacred flame!\nTeldrassil Dun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.5,"y":92.2,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":25.1,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50,"y":72,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"764":{"id":764,"t":"The Venture Co.","lv":10,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 14 Venture Co. Workers and 6 Venture Co. Supervisors for Morin Cloudstalker at Bloodhoof Village.\nVenture Co. Worker slain : 0/ 14\nVenture Co. Supervisor slain : 0/ 6","desc":"This explains the buildup of Venture Co. employees and equipment we've seen in Mulgore. Those goblins... their company is expanding too quickly for their own good. It's how they say, show a goblin something, and you can hear the scales in the background.\nGreedy little things, they are. Unfortunately for their business enterprise, we tauren cannot allow them to conduct their operations in our lands. Go to their mine northeast of the ravaged caravan and send them a message.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The Venture Co. was refused mining rights here in Mulgore, but it would seem that they do not take no for an answer. We tauren are not ones to mince words, however, and we have other ways of getting our message across.","done":"I don't think there could be too much misinterpreting or ignoring of that signal, hm? The Venture Co. will know not to take the tauren lightly, or to be so arrogant as to believe we would allow them to steal the natural resources around us without protest.\nMulgore The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":54.8,"y":64.3,"n":"Morin Cloudstalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9084":{"id":9084,"t":"Bonescythe Bracers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -10g instead of 0.","obj":"Rohan the Assassin at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Bonescythe Bracers if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Bracers, 6 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar, 2 Cured Rugged Hides and 10 gold pieces.\nDesecrated Bracers Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Grand Widow Faerlina 0 % in Naxxramas , Anub'Rekhan 0 % in Naxxramas\n6 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n2 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"If you want Bonescythe made, you're going to have to supply the materials.\nEnter Naxxramas, the big floating city of death in the sky up there, and find desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps. Bring those back along with the materials to put everything together and you'll have your Bonescythe. Oh, and you'll need to pay me for my troubles... I'll supply the bones.","rew":"You will receive:\nBonescythe Bracers\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"How do you expect me to get anything done without the items I requested?","done":"The bracers are ready, ‹name›.\n<Rohan bows.>","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9244":{"id":9244,"t":"Icy Scale Bracers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -200g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 4 Frozen Runes, 16 Heavy Scorpid Scales, 5 Essences of Water, 3 Cured Rugged Hides and 200 gold.\n4 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n16 Heavy Scorpid Scale\n5 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion, may he rest in peace, I am now able to create Icy Scale bracers. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nIcy Scale Bracers","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1644":{"id":1644,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Linen Cloth to Stephanie Turner in Stormwind.\n10 Linen Cloth Kogan Forgestone , Lisan Pierce , Adam Lind 66.7 % , Hidden Strongbox 58.6 % and 4 more","desc":"Bless their hearts, most of them have no families because of the Scourge attacks in the last decade.\nMy husband John collects the materials for me to make the shirts and pants for the children, but I haven't even had time to do that. I've been too focused on keeping food on their plates, and a roof over their heads.\nWhat's that? You'd be willing to help? Oh, thank the Light, and thank you, ‹name›.\nIf you could bring me some linen cloth so I can sew clothes for the kids, that would help me out so much.","rew":"Experience: 900","back":"I hope my John is having better luck in Ironforge. He so dislikes his trips there because it leaves the kids and me alone, but he knows it must be done. He's so kind-hearted.\nSome years have been easier than others, but this one's been rougher by far. It's almost as though something in the air is signaling a huge change. Who knows though?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›, thank you so much!\nThe children will be so pleased, and you've saved me so much time. I'll now be able to focus on the children's other needs, and hopefully my John will be able to return home sooner than we thought.\nThank you again, ‹name›. I knew I could rely on the charity of others. The Light be with you.\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":63.8,"y":72.2,"n":"Stephanie Turner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"96204":{"id":96204,"t":"The windshapers wrath","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Accompany Lumina Windsinger and help her escape Fenris Keep.\nEscort Lumina Windsinger to safety","desc":"Now that I'm free I'm going to make these vile creatures regret ever laying eyes on a Windshaper.\nLet's get out of here, ‹class›.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+50 reputation with Undercity\n+100 reputation with Earthen Ring","done":"Thank you again, Reli. I've been aquatinting myself with Trevan here, who I've learned sent you along on my trail.\nI've heard... less than charitable things about paladins thus far in my travels. As a sky-touched shen'dorei elf traveling through horde territory, I can certainly understand how easily intolerance and prejudice can take root.\nYou and your kind have a friend among the Windshapers.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":65.6,"y":23.2,"n":"Lumina Windsinger","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.2,"y":40.8,"n":"Lumina Windsinger","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"7644":{"id":7644,"t":"Blessed Arcanite Barding","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return with the Blessed Arcanite Barding to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.\nBlessed Arcanite Barding Risen Construct in Scholomance , Petrified Treant\nProvided: Blessed Arcanite Barding","desc":"As the barding rests on the back of the Ancient Equine Spirit, it glows ever so slightly. The air is thick with power for a brief moment, and then the barding disappears from the back of the horse and is now secure in your backpack.\nIt would seem that the barding has been blessed. As per Lord Shadowbreaker's instructions, you should now return with it to him in Stormwind.","back":"‹name›, you're back! Were you able to successfully deal with Merideth Carlson and Tendris Warpwood? Honestly, I'm not sure which one is a greater threat at times...","done":"You've come far, my friend. Your barding is now suitably prepared for the last task at hand.\nYou will be using this barding to harness your charger once the task of redemption is complete. Before that, however, you will have a monumental struggle to overcome. Your time draws near - huzzah!\nThere is one last item that needs to be made before we begin this, ‹name›. Hopefully your resourcefulness has not departed you since you had your barding made...","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5644":{"id":5644,"t":"Devouring Plague","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Devouring Plague.","obj":"Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity.","desc":"Ah, a wonderful day for you, ‹name›. I can see by the lessons you've learned that the time has come to send you back to Aelthalyste. There are things only she can teach you, and even then, only if you prove worthy.\nI will not spoil the surprise for you, but I remember when I was a young priest learning about true power... divine power. Yes, those were the days.\nGo back to Aelthalyste in the Undercity, ‹name›. She will be awaiting you in the War Quarter.","rew":"You will learn: Devouring Plague\nExperience: 390","done":"I would teach you Devouring Plague if you feel you are prepared, ‹name›. A spell of no small power, it will aid you in your coming battles. Practice with it--there will be tests later.\nOrgrimmar Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.7,"y":86.9,"n":"Zayus","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49.3,"y":17.1,"n":"Aelthalyste","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"5724":{"id":5724,"t":"Returning the Lost Satchel","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,950 experience instead of 1,450, 2.03 times as much. New rewards: Garrison Cuffs. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a norm","obj":"Take the Grimtotem Satchel to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.\nGrimtotem Satchel\nProvided: Grimtotem Satchel","desc":"You find a satchel under the body of the tauren. It is still gripped tightly in his arms as though he was trying to protect it while being attacked by the troggs.\nRemoving the satchel from his vice-like grip, you stow it with your own equipment and prepare to make your way out of the tunnels and back to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFeatherbead Bracers Savannah Bracers Garrison Cuffs\nNew in Forever: Garrison Cuffs.\nExperience: 2,950\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Were you able to find anything, ‹name›? Any clues as to why one of her clansman had to die needlessly would be helpful.","done":"Excellent, ‹name›. Thank you.\nMagatha told me that if you were successful in finding her clansman that you be given this. Please, take it in thanks.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":70.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Rahauro","e":1}],"cats":["ragefire-chasm"]},"124":{"id":124,"t":"A Baying of Gnolls","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Redridge Brutes and 8 Redridge Mystics, then return to Verner Osgood.\nRedridge Brute slain : 0/ 10\nRedridge Mystic slain : 0/ 8","desc":"As if the attacking orcs weren't enough! Now I have gnoll brutes and mystics prowling along the ridge north of my stable, taking my horses when they stray...\nIf you can get rid of those gnolls, my horses and I would be very grateful.","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes? Is there something I can do for you?","done":"Thank you for all your help, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":25.9,"y":47.3,"n":"Verner Osgood","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8844":{"id":8844,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horde Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with the Darkspear tribe.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":46.3,"y":35.1,"n":"Officer Vu'Shalay","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"7724":{"id":7724,"t":"Fiery Menace!","lv":49,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hansel Heavyhands wants you to kill 20 Greater Lava Spiders in the Searing Gorge. You can find Greater Lava Spiders in the plateaus and lava pools of the Searing Gorge.\nReturn to Hansel Heavyhands in the Searing Gorge when you have killed enough Greater Lava Spiders.\nSearing Lava Spider slain : 0/ 20","desc":"Wouldn't ye know it, every time ol' Hansel wants to take a moment to relax and reflect upon his life, the powers that be give him another job.\nMe gots to think, come on! Ye know what I be saying? Come. On.\nSo, these here greater lava spiders are causin' a ruckus o' some sort. Oilfist says they shoot fire out their... erm, yea well, anyway, such things upset the children.\nI guess we gots to kill 'em. Rather, ye gots to kill 'em.","rew":"You will receive:\nSeared Mail Girdle\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"Was he right? Does it come out their rumps?","done":"<Hansel sneezes.>\nI think I'm gettin' a cold. Damn this frigid climate!","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.6,"y":27.8,"n":"Hansel Heavyhands","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"3084":{"id":3084,"t":"Rune-Inscribed Tablet","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Shikrik in the Valley of Trials.\nRune-Inscribed Tablet\nProvided: Rune-Inscribed Tablet","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the shaman trainer Shikrik. She would have words with you when you're ready.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Ah, welcome, ‹name›. I'm pleased you have arrived. My days have become long and even busy what with so many students to teach, but the coming of one of your ilk brings me a great sense of accomplishment--I remember the days when I was taught by one of your shamans.","done":"As you probably know, the elements give us our power. Fire, earth, water and air--these are our tools.\nOur strength comes from the spirits of our ancestors. We are the leaders of our people. Like Thrall is to the Horde, so shall we be to the villages and towns we visit. They will look to us for wisdom and protection. To be better prepared, you must train often. When you feel you've gained more power, come to me and I shall teach you what I can.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":69,"n":"Shikrik","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"97244":{"id":97244,"t":"Call of fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay Skypriest Faladiel in the Gustberry Lowlands and collect Faladiel's Heart.\nFaladiel's Heart","desc":"There is an Al'Aketh Skypriest called Faladiel. He was once a caller of the flame and a stalwart Windshaper. Like so many Al'Aketh, he mortgaged his loyalty for power and his hands are now stained with the blood of his former brothers and sisters.\nYou will find Skypriest Faladiel at the farm to the northeast past Valanaar, just to the south of the Shrine of Akir. Kill the betrayer. Bring me his heart. It is a gruesome task, but it is needed for the ritual we are to perform.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+25 reputation with Windshapers","back":"The heart of a betrayer is a powerful reagent. The flames will eagerly accept such an offering and burn more intensely as it is consumed.","done":"The Windshapers do not forget, and blood is always paid with blood. It pleases me that you were able to deliver this final, painful reminder of our creed to this traitor.\nThis heart will not be all that feeds the flames today, however. There is one other task that needs to done.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":51.2,"y":86,"n":"Olariaan Swiftburn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"92844":{"id":92844,"t":"Mountain of bones","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\nGently Cursed Bone x 426\nMagram Clan Centaur:","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,450\n+500 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\nLevel 42 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 38 40 45 53 Side Both factions Quest ID 92844\nThe chain\n15 quests from level 32 to 43, 36,630 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n[ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n10 [ 43 ] Bristleback Retreat\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristleback Retreat.\n3,600 XP\n11 [ 43 ] Long-Term Solutions\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram clan and slay 2 Outcast Scouts, 6 Outcast Marauders, and 8 Outcast Necromancers then return to Hagiak at the Magram","cats":["shendralas"]},"6844":{"id":6844,"t":"Umber, Archivist","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Encrusted Silithid Object to Umber - the Cenarion Circle's archivist - in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.\nEncrusted Silithid Object Hive'Ashi Ambusher\nProvided: Encrusted Silithid Object","desc":"There's plenty to do here still, but I think taking this back to the Circle for analysis is key. Trust me - the work will still be here once this is all said and done. If it's a journal inside this sticky chitin, then the Circle would finally have a window into the past!\nTake this to the Circle's archivist in Nighthaven. His name is Umber, and the man's brilliant. Touched, sure, but brilliant nonetheless! Umber's salvaged tomes in far worse shape than this. If it can be saved, he can do it.","rew":"Experience: 3,000\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Why, hello there! Hrmm...\nLet me be a little honest with you, friend... you smell a bit ripe. Whiffy, one might say. Now I'm not making a personal assailment of your being. I'm just saying... in the future, you may want to freshen up a little after coming in from the field. It will make those first impressions a little more positively impressionable!\nAnyhoo... what can I do for you?","done":"Well great monkey toads! What have you got here? It's sort of book shaped, I guess... I'll try crack this shell on it.\nLayo sent you to me from Silithus? I've only heard very hushed rumblings - which I guess aren't all that hushed when you think about it - about the horrors that are going on out there. Couple that with my lack of pleasure for anything bug-like, and you've got the recipe for me needing to stay here with the books!\nSilithus Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":81.9,"y":18.9,"n":"Layo Starstrike","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":44.9,"y":35.6,"n":"Umber","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8284":{"id":8284,"t":"The Twilight Mystery","lv":58,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to collect 8 Twilight Tablet Fragments.\n8 Twilight Tablet Fragment Twilight Tablet Fragment , Twilight Tablet Fragment , Whirling Invader 5 %","desc":"A camp of Twilight's Hammer cultists once thrived northwest of here. If you were to venture there now, you'd find the area swarming with elementals and nothing but scattered pieces of wood and canvas to mark the spot where the camp was.\nI've recovered a few fragments of a clay tablet from the site, but I have too few of them to piece together anything useful. See if you can find the remaining tablet fragments so we can shed some light into the Twilight's Hammer presence here in Silithus.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"The ravaged camp can be found northwest of here. Come back when you have all the fragments.","done":"Just as I suspected. I can decipher individual words in the tablets but they appear to be devoid of any logic or meaning. It's not unknown for Twilight's Hammer sects to use a code to hide the meaning of their texts; we'll have to go to someone who knows more about this sort of thing.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8364":{"id":8364,"t":"Abyssal Scepters","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,300 experience instead of 3,500, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"3 Abyssal Scepter Prince Skaldrenox , High Marshal Whirlaxis , Baron Kazum , Lord Skwol","rew":"You will receive:\nChest of Spoils\nExperience: 3,300\n+150 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You've truly exceeded all my expectations, ‹name›. You've been taking on opponents that Huum and I would think long and hard before engaging.\nAt this point the best I can do is to continue rewarding your efforts in the fight against the Twilight's Hammer and their overlords.\nBring me more abyssal scepters and I'll do my best to give you a suitable reward.","done":"I knew you'd come through, ‹name›! Here's your reward.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"444":{"id":444,"t":"Rot Hide Origins","lv":17,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Sample Ichor to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.\nSample Ichor\nProvided: Sample Ichor","desc":"I have reduced the ichor you brought me and separated it into its base components. My findings are not conclusive, but I have determined that warlock and necromantic magics were used in the ichor's creation.\nWhile I continue to study the ichor, I want you to take a sample to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity. Bethor is not an apothecary, but his knowledge of magic may help to unravel the mystery of the rot hides.\nGo. You will find Bethor in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.","rew":"Experience: 320\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"My studies require great concentration. So I hope your visit is not a frivolous one.","done":"This substance is laced with powerful spells, some of which I have not seen for a long, long time...\nOne moment -- I must invoke a spell of divination...\nSilverpine Forest Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":84.1,"y":17.4,"n":"Bethor Iceshard","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"95884":{"id":95884,"t":"The offering stone","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the Offering Stone in Beren's Peril in Silverpine Forest.\nNote Scrap","desc":"<The scrap of note is mostly illegible. What is still readable, however, are notes about preparations for an offering.\nAn offering stone is mentioned, as well as a ritual.\nPerhaps you can find this offering stone nearby.>","done":"<Strange implements and items litter the rough surface of the stone.\nThis is surely the offering stone that is mentioned in the note.>","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":58.1,"y":69.9,"n":"Offering Stone","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"78124":{"id":78124,"t":"Narthalas almanac","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Nar'thalas Almanac, Vol. 74","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nNar'thalas Almanac, Vol. 74 (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"6284":{"id":6284,"t":"Arachnophobia","lv":21,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Besseleth and bring Besseleth's Fang to Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat.\nBesseleth's Fang Besseleth","desc":"Warning: Proceed into Sishir Canyon west of here at your own risk.\nBesseleth and her eight-legged children of the forest have claimed this canyon as their webbed lair.\nMaggran Earthbinder in Sun Rock Retreat has placed a bounty on Besseleth. Slay her and bring proof of your killing to Maggran; there you will receive your reward for disposing this eight-legged menace.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nClaystone Shortsword Clear Crystal Rod\nExperience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Besseleth is a ruthless predator... I fear for those that travel Webwinder Path at night. It's then that she and her children prey upon innocent travelers. I myself fell prey to her two-foot fang of death, but luckily I was able to fend her off and get to safety. I would give anything to see that monster destroyed.","done":"Good hunting, ‹name›! Besseleth is an old predator in these parts... I will miss her not. Take this reward as a token for being the forest champion.\n<Maggran rubs the wound caused by Besseleth.>\nPerhaps now many more will travel to Sun Rock Retreat without fearing what lurks in the dark.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.1,"y":75.7,"n":"Wanted Poster: Besseleth","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":47.2,"y":61.2,"n":"Maggran Earthbinder","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1084":{"id":1084,"t":"Wounded Ancients","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a piece of Corroded Shrapnel to Kaela Shadowspear in Stonetalon.\nCorroded Shrapnel Blackened Ancient 20 % , Charred Ancient 20 % , Vengeful Ancient 20 %","desc":"It seems obvious to me that the protectors of the Vale--the treants--had something to do with the Venture Co. being driven back. Unfortunately, even those once great guardians have now become corrupt.\nGaxim thinks their corruption is somehow linked to the weapons the goblins used during their retreat.\nI told him I'd collect a sample from a wounded treant and allow him to study it in order to figure out if that's true.\nBring me some of the shrapnel so the gnome can tell me more...","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"I have a feeling Gaxim will find a use for the shrapnel regardless of how the Venture Co. has used it in the past.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›.\nThis should be more than sufficient for Gaxim to figure out how the treants were corrupted. I shall give this to him right away.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.9,"y":66.8,"n":"Kaela Shadowspear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"1244":{"id":1244,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":30,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Defias Docket and return it to Watcher Backus in Duskwood.\nDefias Docket Defias Strongbox","desc":"Defias activity? Well, there's always some activity; even if they keep to themselves we consider them a threat.\nBut now that I think about it, there was a recent sighting that seemed odd. It must have been a couple weeks ago, but some of their agents had gathered around Addle's Stead. From the report, I'd guessed something big went down.\nWhy don't you check there first and bring me back anything you find?\nThe farmstead is south of the road from Westfall just as you enter Duskwood.","rew":"Experience: 2,450","back":"Be careful out there, ‹name›. I know Trias was the one to send you here, but that doesn't mean there isn't anything lurking out in the woods that couldn't cause you some trouble... especially with you investigating the Defias.","done":"You're back safe and sound. Couldn't ask for much more than that, could you?\nNow, let's see what we have here. This looks pretty official as far as any Defias documents I've seen. But it could be a dupe just to throw you off track of whatever it is you're looking for.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":74.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Watcher Backus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"1324":{"id":1324,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":38,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat Private Hendel in Dustwallow Marsh.","desc":"What?! You come here accusing me of allying with the Defias, and think I'll just stand here while you insult me?! Something tells me you've had this coming for a long time.","rew":"Experience: 2,150\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello again, ‹name›. I hope you don't mind the assistance, but we couldn't have Hendel escaping, or worse, wind up dead.","done":"I assure you, we're all quite upset about current events, but allow us to take him back to Theramore for some questioning, and we'll see about finding the King.\nI'm sure my lady Proudmore would like to thank you for your help. Speak to her when you have a moment.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":45.2,"y":24.7,"n":"Private Hendel","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Archmage Tervosh","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"204":{"id":204,"t":"Bad Medicine","lv":34,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 7 Jungle Remedies and 1 Venom Fern Extract to Sergeant Yohwa at the Rebel Camp.\n7 Jungle Remedy Kurzen Witch Doctor 35.6 % , Kurzen Jungle Fighter 35 % , Kurzen Medicine Man 34.4 % , Kurzen Headshrinker 33.3 %\nVenom Fern Extract Kurzen Supplies , Kurzen Supplies","desc":"To have a chance against Kurzen, we need his healing support neutralized. He has gathered a large number of Medicine Men who heal his forces with Jungle Remedies and poison our fighters with Venom Fern Extracts.\nWe need those remedies and extracts for our own. Search the Kurzen Compound - his Medicine Men and Jungle fighers will have the remedies, and the extracts are probably stowed in some of the camp's supply boxes.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPalm Frond Mantle Guerrilla Cleaver\nExperience: 2,700\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I'm waiting on those remedies and that extract, ‹name›.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. These remedies will keep more of us alive and in fighting shape. And the extracts will help us create our own remedies.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38,"y":3.3,"n":"Sergeant Yohwa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"604":{"id":604,"t":"The Bloodsail Buccaneers","lv":43,"min":37,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay wants you to kill 10 Bloodsail Swashbucklers and bring back the Bloodsail Charts and the Bloodsail Orders.\nBloodsail Charts Bloodsail Charts\nBloodsail Orders Bloodsail Orders\nBloodsail Swashbuckler slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Crazz speaks highly of your dedication to the Blackwater Raiders. I am going to trust you with a mission of extreme importance to the fleet.\nInfiltrate the so-called southern command post the Bloodsail Buccaneers have established on the Wild Shore. Raid the encampment. Bring me their charts along with their written orders. We shall see exactly what those scum are up to.","rew":"Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Ahoy, ‹name›. What word do you bring of the Bloodsail encampment to the south?","done":"Perfect, ‹name›. Now that we know their plan, it's just a matter of time.\nAnd to think the fools have dropped anchor just off the cape....","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":77,"n":"Fleet Master Seahorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8924":{"id":8924,"t":"Hunting for Ectoplasm","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Ectoplasmic Distiller near incorporeal undead to collect 12 Scorched Ectoplasms in Silithus, 12 Frozen Ectoplasms in Winterspring and 12 Stable Ectoplasms in the Eastern Plaguelands. Bring them along with the Ectoplasmic Distiller back to Mux Manascrambler in Gadgetzan.\n12 Scorched Ectoplasm Tortured Sentinel 80 % , Tortured Druid 80 %\n12 Frozen Ectoplasm Anguished Highborne 80 % , Suffering Highborne 80 %\n12 Stable Ectoplasm Death Singer 80 % , Hate Shrieker 80 % , Torn Screamer 80 % , Eyeless Watcher 80 % and 1 more\nEctoplasmic Distiller\nProvided: Ectoplasmic Distiller","desc":"A fine piece of engineering, if I do say so myself! You will need to travel a bit, I'm afraid, in order to find the incorporeal undead we require.\nYou see, different climates lend different consistencies to the spectral fabric of the dead. The tortured night elves of Silithus, the spirits of the highborne from Winterspring and the ghosts and banshees of the Eastern Plaguelands should give us the different types of ectoplasm we need. Be sure to place the distiller nearby before you harvest them!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600","back":"Have you gathered the ectoplasm yet, ‹race›?","done":"Yes, these will do great!\nBy tapping into the otherworldly energies contained within these substances we'll be able to reach out to those whose souls haven't quite left this world yet!\nTanaris Silithus Winterspring Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Mux Manascrambler","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8764":{"id":8764,"t":"The Changing of Paths - Protector No More","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\n15 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n15 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n15 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","back":"Champion, should you decide to walk another path, present me with your signet ring and a mountain of scarabs from our enemies in Ahn'Qiraj.","done":"Be well, ‹name›. If you change your mind, I shall be here to assist you.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"6364":{"id":6364,"t":"Return to Jahan","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Buy a wind rider to the Crossroads from the wind rider master Tal, then bring Ahanu's Leather Goods to Jahan Hawkwing.\nAhanu's Leather Goods\nProvided: Ahanu's Leather Goods","desc":"In order to fly to a town, you must have already been there and spoken with the wind rider master of that town. You have been to the Crossroads and spoken to their wind rider master Devrak, so for a small fee you can take a wind rider to him from here.\nSpeak with me again when you are ready. Once at the Crossroads, you can then deliver the leather goods to Jahan Hawkwing.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 1,050\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"‹name›, you are back from Thunder Bluff? Did you deliver the hides to Ahanu?","done":"Ahanu sent me finished products? Very good. There are many hunters and adventurers in the Crossroads now and business is lively. I am sure I'll sell these goods very soon.\nThank you for all your efforts, ‹name›. I am in your debt.\nThunder Bluff The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":47,"y":49.8,"n":"Tal","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.2,"y":29,"n":"Jahan Hawkwing","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"844":{"id":844,"t":"Plainstrider Menace","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 7 Plainstrider Beaks and return them to Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.\n7 Plainstrider Beak Greater Plainstrider 80 % , Ornery Plainstrider 80 % , Fleeting Plainstrider 80 %","desc":"Your first prey will be easy.\nThe plainstriders to the east have been harassing our food supplies and have become a nuisance.\nPut down the plainstriders and return to me with their beaks.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you collected the plainstrider beaks?","done":"Very good, ‹name›. With the plainstriders gone we'll have an easier time keeping our supply chains intact. And I hope you learned a few tricks out there in the Barrens, for your next prey has a little more fire in its blood than the plainstriders...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31,"n":"Sergra Darkthorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"3804":{"id":3804,"t":"Morrowgrain to Thunder Bluff","lv":55,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Morrowgrain","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Circle Cache\nExperience: 550\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The Arch Druid is always looking for more morrowgrain for the Cenarion Circle's research project on Un'Goro Crater. We take them in increments of ten, and award you with a cache of goods you should find useful. When you have ten, let me know and I will award you accordingly.","done":"Excellent - this morrowgrain will no doubt help when the time comes. We know that the night elves are conducting similar research into these herbs, though it isn't clear to what end they will use them for if they discover anything. The Arch Druid thinks that the need for morrowgrain will remain until we've figured out the mysteries behind this herb.\nThis is for you, ‹name›. The Cenarion Circle thanks you for your continued support.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":34.2,"n":"Bashana Runetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"364":{"id":364,"t":"The Mindless Ones","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Shadow Priest Sarvis wants you to kill 8 Mindless Zombies and 8 Wretched Zombies.\nMindless Zombie slain : 0/ 8\nWretched Zombie slain : 0/ 8","desc":"We Forsaken are at war with the Lich King's army of the Scourge: necromantically raised armies of the undead, foul beasts of the north, and tormented spectres.\nThe northern part of the village has become overrun with the Mindless Ones, and they must be destroyed. Destroy them, show them no mercy, our former brothers and sisters as they might be. The Fallen are nothing but The Lich King's slaves.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFlax Gloves Battered Cloak\nMoney: 17 0 gold, 0 silver, 17 copper Experience: 170\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"You will not go far in this new life if you are unable to kill even the weakest of zombies, ‹name›. Do not return until you have success to report.","done":"It is unfortunate that the Scourge cannot be brought into the fold, their large numbers would be useful in the battles ahead.\nBut they will not join us, so we have no choice but to destroy them.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.8,"y":66.2,"n":"Shadow Priest Sarvis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2284":{"id":2284,"t":"Necklace Recovery, Take 2","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find a clue as to the gems' whereabouts in the depths of Uldaman.","desc":"As sure as Malton is a dummy, those gems are still in Uldaman somewhere. You're going to have to go back there and look for them.\nLike I said before, if the information we have is correct then there's a ruby, a sapphire, and a topaz that go with the necklace. Find them and put them in the necklace.\nAs to where the gems are, who knows? Maybe you'll get lucky and find the corpse of the Paladin. If he's not been stripped clean already, then maybe he's got them on him still.","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"You seem to have found the remains of the paladin that Dran had mentioned from before. Searching the remains uncovers what would appear to be his journal. The book is in poor condition, as dried blood has stained most of the text in the book. What you can read, however, is gibberish; it is written in the native tongue of the humans, to the best of your knowledge.\nYou will need the book translated if you are to glean any knowledge from it.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":59.6,"y":36.5,"n":"Dran Droffers","s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"2204":{"id":2204,"t":"Restoring the Necklace","lv":44,"min":37,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain a power source from the most powerful construct you can find in Uldaman, and deliver it to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.\nShattered Necklace Power Source Archaedas","desc":"You are going to need to find some \"oomph\" for the necklace, and Uldaman is probably the best place for it, actually. I guess there are a lot of constructs running around in there, yeah? Well, take out the biggest, baddest construct in that place and grab its power source! I am pretty sure I can fuse that source into the necklace.\nWithout that power source, fixing the necklace will be impossible. Come back to me here to Ironforge when you have it, and we'll get it all fixed up for you!","rew":"Experience: 925","back":"You didn't even stop to tidy yourself up after leaving Uldaman, did you. You just came straight here, lingering dungeon odors be damned. Well, let's hope this visit is merely an odiferous one, and not a useless one to boot.\nDo you have the power source for the necklace?","done":"Well I'll be - I sure am glad to see you and this power source in one piece. It will take me a moment to magically fuse the power source with the necklace now that the gems have been reunited with it. Once it is done, however, the necklace will be yours!\nYou're excited, aren't you? All tingly with anticipation? Now where did I put that spell focus at...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Talvash del Kissel","e":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"3884":{"id":3884,"t":"Williden's Journal","lv":50,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the journal to Williden Marshal somewhere in Un'Goro Crater.\nA Mangled Journal Ravasaur Runner 4.5 % , Ravasaur 4 % , Thunderstomp Stegodon 3 % , Venomhide Ravasaur 2.9 % and 4 more\nProvided: A Mangled Journal","desc":"You have uncovered a mangled journal. Parts of it remain legible, with a Williden Marshal claiming ownership over the contents therein. If the journal is accurate, then Williden may be found somewhere in the northern part of the Crater; according to the journal, he and his companions sought higher ground from the savage beasts of the Crater once their base camps were overrun.","rew":"Experience: 3,550","back":"Hello there! I and my companions are happy to see some living beings here other than overgrown savage beasts! What brings you into the Un'Goro Crater?","done":"Well look at this - my journal! I thought it was lost, much like almost everything else we brought into Un'Goro. I thank you kindly for returning this to me!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":43.9,"y":7.1,"n":"Williden Marshal","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4284":{"id":4284,"t":"Crystals of Power","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 7 Power Crystals of each color: red, blue, yellow, and green. Bring them to J.D. Collie at Marshal's Refuge.\n7 Red Power Crystal Red Power Crystal , Red Power Crystal , Mor'vek 46.2 % , Stegodon 0.4 % and 4 more\n7 Yellow Power Crystal Yellow Power Crystal , Yellow Power Crystal , Mor'vek 66.7 % , Gruff 0.6 % and 4 more\n7 Green Power Crystal Green Power Crystal , Green Power Crystal , Mor'vek 30.8 % , Spiked Stegodon 0.4 % and 4 more\n7 Blue Power Crystal Blue Power Crystal , Blue Power Crystal , Mor'vek 25.6 % , Plated Stegodon 0.3 % and 4 more","desc":"I'm sure you've noticed 'em, ‹name›. They're everywhere!\nWhat am I talking about? Why, the crystals, of course!\nThe crystals... They're all over the crater. Most people ignore them, but I have a strange feeling that they hold power within them. I've been doing experiments here with them for a while, but I can't seem to find anything. Well, I haven't yet, anyway.\nSay, I'm running a little low on the crystals I have here -- think you might be able to collect some more for me?","rew":"Money: 80 0 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,250","back":"I just know I'm onto something here, ‹name›!","done":"Now I will continue my experiments! Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":41.9,"y":2.7,"n":"J.D. Collie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1164":{"id":1164,"t":"To Steal From Thieves","lv":36,"min":27,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Kenata, Fardel, and Marcel Dabyrie's Heads to Genavie Callow in Undercity.\nKenata's Head Kenata Dabyrie\nMarcel's Head Marcel Dabyrie\nFardel's Head Fardel Dabyrie","desc":"The harlot! The swine! Kenata still lives; her family healthy and prospering while I suffer. Forsaken indeed!\nMy family is gone, taken by the plague. Our estate also forfeit; looted and burned during the war. And after all that, her and her lousy children had the audacity to steal the only precious belongings I had left.\nI don't care about the things they stole any more. What I want now are their heads!\nKill them for me! Go to the Dabyrie Farmstead in Arathi, northeast of Refuge Point.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGrim Pauldrons Gallan Cuffs\nExperience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Kill them all and bring me their heads!","done":"You stand before me as a figure of vengeance, and I bow down before you in thanks.\nWith that cow's death, and knowing that their seed will no longer spread over the face of Azeroth, I can put my energy into something more lucrative. I hope you looted their farmstead after you finished them off.\nUndercity Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":63.8,"y":49.5,"n":"Genavie Callow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1004":{"id":1004,"t":"The New Frontier","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.","desc":"Attention, heroes!\nThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor! A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.\nAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle. Speak with the Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder's Rise of Thunder Bluff for more information!","rew":"Experience: 550\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Greetings, ‹class›.\nI am pleased to see the likes of you taking an interest in the well being of nature; tales of your mighty deeds precede you, and you are welcomed here. Seeing you before me instills the feeling of confidence that the Cenarion Circle will get the proper aid it needs.\nOur connection with the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade transcends racial and political divides. Remember this as you work on behalf of the Circle, and you will do well.\nUndercity Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":63.9,"y":44.1,"n":"Harbinger Balthazad","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1804":{"id":1804,"t":"Tome of the Cabal","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Reconstructed Tome and 3 Rods of Channeling to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.\nReconstructed Tome\n3 Rod of Channeling Dragonmaw Bonewarder 80 % , Dragonmaw Shadowwarder 80 %\nProvided: Reconstructed Tome","desc":"Well, ah, it's hard to let it go. But you found it, and you have more important things to do with it, of course. Just, please, be sure to mention to Strahad that I wanted a copy.\nWhile you were out, he sent a message for you. He wanted me to tell you that for his acolytes to assist with the summoning, you'll have to acquire three rods of channeling.\nHe might not know where to find them, but I do! They were last used by the orcs of the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands. I'd check their spellcasters!","rew":"Experience: 2,450","back":"Haven't seen you around these parts for a while. Have you found the tome and the rods?","done":"Well done! The Tome of the Cabal and three pristine--slightly scratched, I suppose--rods of channeling.\nThis will be interesting. It's been some time since a young warlock took on a felhunter to make his own.\nDun Morogh The Barrens Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":22.6,"n":"Krom Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7564":{"id":7564,"t":"Wildeyes","lv":58,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Case of Blood to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.\nCase of Blood\nProvided: Case of Blood","desc":"My servant, Gorzeeki, is an alchemist of some skill. He can prepare the ink I will need for your parchment. I gathered together the blood you acquired; take it to Gorzeeki so that he can begin his work.","rew":"Experience: 3,100","back":"You have something for me? It's not a big, juicy spider, is it? Or maybe a roach? I hope it's still alive... I so love chewing on them when they're still alive...","done":"Oh, it's blood. It must be from master Mor'zul then. He is so enamored with the stuff, and loves to see it spilled. I, however, prefer it coursing through the veins of a small rodent. It stays warm that way... until you want it.\nThis is powerful blood. Mor'zul must be making another parchment to summon a dreadsteed! How exciting!\nIf that's true, and you're going to perform the ritual, then... you're going to need a lot more than blood, my friend.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.7,"y":31.6,"n":"Mor'zul Bloodbringer","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Gorzeeki Wildeyes","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"5404":{"id":5404,"t":"Corruptor's Scourgestones","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Corruptor's Scourgestone Darkmaster Gandling , Marduk Blackpool in Scholomance , Hed'mush the Rotting , Lord Darkscythe and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Valor Token\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"A Corruptor's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's overlords. A powerful being that holds a position of authority over the Scourge will always possess one. To slay such a malevolent creature would surely advance the cause of the Argent Dawn, and all good causes!\nOn behalf of the Argent Dawn, I will give you a valor token in exchange for just a single one these insignia. Use caution in acquiring one, ‹name› - such powerful beings are not to be trifled with.","done":"Congratulations, ‹name› - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!\nTo acquire a valor token in such a manner indicates that you are a true hero in the cause of good. We value all effort brought to bear against the Scourge, but to take down one of their leaders is to truly deliver onto them a crushing defeat!\nFor the Dawn, my brother/sister!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":83.5,"n":"Argent Officer Pureheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5804":{"id":5804,"t":"Araj's Scarab","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy Araj the Summoner and bring Araj's Scarab to Apothecary Dithers at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nAraj's Scarab Araj's Phylactery","desc":"Araj the Summoner lords over Andorhal from the ruined city's heart. We know that he was the former leader of Scholomance before claiming the city as his own. To finish the key, we will need his signet - called a scarab - mounted as the head of the key.\nMake your way into the heart of Andorhal, and break his hold on the city now that he is drawn into the open. Once destroyed, seize his scarab from his fallen phylactery!\nThe Key to Scholomance awaits, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 4,950","back":"You've come this far ‹name› - only the destruction of the physical form of Araj the Summoner will provide us with the means to finish the key. Get Araj's scarab, by hook or by crook, and bring it to me - I will fuse it on as the head of the key.","done":"Yes, this is it! I... again, I'm absolutely amazed at the depths of your cunning and bravery. It simply boggles the mind the lengths you are willing to go in order achieve victory.\nAllow me now to play my small part in this. I've prepared a special solvent that should allow me to secure the scarab on as the head of the key, infusing it with the power to breech the locked door of Scholomance.\nThis should take just a moment...\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":69.2,"n":"Apothecary Dithers","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5164":{"id":5164,"t":"Catalogue of the Wayward","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 700, 0.93 times as much.","obj":"Read from the Catalogue of the Wayward.","desc":"A finer instrument of justice, Haleh could not have chosen. Read from the catalogue of the wayward and be enlightened.\nShould you persist... should you do what is asked of you... should you survive... a hero you will make.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Hundreds upon hundreds of pages filled with garbled text and symbols make up the brunt of this book.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.4,"y":66.8,"n":"Jeziba","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.3,"y":66.6,"n":"Catalogue of the Wayward","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"284":{"id":284,"t":"The Search Continues","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search for the Menethil Statuette.","desc":"You thoroughly search this cluster of Murloc hovels, and find no trace of the Menethil Statuette.\nPerhaps one of the two nearby hovels to the north and northeast will have more clues.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Dwarven Mild\nExperience: 500\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"This barrel is largely untouched. Prying it open...\n...you are assaulted by the pungent odor of cheese. It's a little wet, but still tasty!","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":13.5,"y":41.4,"n":"Damaged Crate","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":13.6,"y":38.2,"n":"Sealed Barrel","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"5084":{"id":5084,"t":"Falling to Corruption","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the Deadwood furbolg camp in northern Felwood for a clue.","desc":"This greenish liquid... it reminds me a bit of the sludge I saw when traveling through Felwood. And I have seen some Winterfall Runners passing into Timbermaw... Perhaps these things have something to do with the flask you found, ‹name›.\nThere is a large group of furbolg just past Timbermaw Hold, in Felwood. Called the Deadwood tribe, they have been corrupted and driven mad by the fel. Why don't you look around there and see if you can find any evidence of dealings between the Winterfall and the Deadwood?","rew":"Experience: 4,350\n+75 reputation with Everlook","done":"Inside the cauldron bubbles a rotting, repulsive-smelling substance...\nWinterspring Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":60.2,"y":5.8,"n":"Deadwood Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5244":{"id":5244,"t":"The Ruins of Kel'Theril","lv":56,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Jaron Stoneshaper in Starfall Village.","desc":"The story behind Kel'Theril is one of a cursed race, bound to the place where they attempted an unfortunate ritual...\nThe highborne that you will find there once stole a sacred artifact, believing that they could siphon its power for themselves, becoming even more powerful. In their efforts, the relic shattered in a huge explosion, driving the pieces below the ice of the lake...\nSpeak with Jaron Stoneshaper if you'd like to learn more; he has recently visited the area and can tell you more.","rew":"Experience: 575\n+10 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Well, sure, I can tell you more about Kel'Theril. Mind you now, I'm no historian, but I can tell ya about what I saw there...","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":52,"y":30.4,"n":"Wynd Nightchaser","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":52.1,"y":30.4,"n":"Jaron Stoneshaper","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"6604":{"id":6604,"t":"Enraged Wildkin","lv":59,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Jaron Stoneshaper at Starfall Village.","desc":"Have you noticed the abandoned camp to the south of here? It looks like the wildkin went crazy and destroyed just about everything they could find!\nI heard a rumor that one of the survivors of the attack is resting at Starfall Village, west of here. I'm sure curious about what happened... aren't you?","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"Aye, what can I do for you?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.1,"y":38.4,"n":"Harlo Wigglesworth","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":52.1,"y":30.4,"n":"Jaron Stoneshaper","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92684":{"id":92684,"t":"Ornery ornery galestriders","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 7 Lowlands Galestrider Tenderloins from the Ornery Galestriders found throughout the Gustberry Lowlands.\n7 Lowlands Galestrider Tenderloin","desc":"As if the harvest wasn't light enough this year already, the galestriders in the area have been getting into the orchard and stealing my stormapples. Think you can head out to the fields and cull them for me?\nTake care though stranger, these lowlands galestriders are bigger and angrier than the highlands variety. Watch yourself. A well timed kick is all it takes to put you down for good if you aren't paying attention.\nBring me some of their meat and I can make us a hot meal with it as well.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFarmer's Field Boots Brass-Banded Bracers Well-Worn Pants\nYou will also receive:\n5 Red Delicious Stormapple\nExperience: 600","back":"I don't think I've had real meat for dinner in... well, too long.","done":"These are big tenderloins! You must have taken down some real monsters out there.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.6,"y":81.8,"n":"Aamelia Windfield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8044":{"id":8044,"t":"The Rage of Mount Mugamba","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from The Rage of Mount Mugamba. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Strength of Mugamba","rew":"You will receive:\nRage of Mugamba\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"King Rastakhan sends his regards, Master ‹name›. Such an honor has never been given to one outside the Zandalar tribe.\n<Jin'rokh bows.>\nGive me your talisman so that I may enhance it once more. Know that the Rage of Mugamba is now intrinsically connected to your very soul.","done":"Zul'jin would be envious, ‹class›. Go forth and conquer!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});